# Quality Assurance

## Code Quality Checklist

### Python Code
- [ ] Follows PEP 8 style guide
- [ ] Clear variable names (educational focus)
- [ ] Comprehensive comments explaining concepts
- [ ] Proper error handling with learner-friendly messages
- [ ] Code is executable and produces expected outputs
- [ ] No linting errors

### Jupyter Notebooks
- [ ] Markdown cells provide clear explanations
- [ ] Code cells are well-commented
- [ ] Outputs are included for demonstration
- [ ] Logical flow from simple to complex
- [ ] All cells execute without errors
- [ ] Visualizations are clear and labeled

## Content Quality Requirements

- All educational content must be original (ZERO copy policy)
- Examples must be practical and relevant
- Progressive difficulty maintained
- Concepts explained clearly for learners
- Real-world applications demonstrated
- Common pitfalls documented

## Documentation Quality

- README.md accurately describes repository structure
- Learning paths are clear and documented
- Code examples are well-explained
- Module documentation is current
- Cross-references are valid
- File references point to existing files
